  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "The lead changed hands three times. They held the last one for exactly two innings.",
    "what_this_means": "Bericoto's two-run homer in the sixth put them up 8-4. That looked like the game. Oakland answered in the seventh, then came back with four more in the ninth. A comeback Giants pitching couldn't survive. Roupp gave them six solid innings, but Ryan Walker and Caleb Kilian combined to give up six earned runs in less than an inning of work. The offense did its part: five hits became three runs on two RISP conversions, and Adames added another homer. It was not enough. A two-run lead lasted 120 pitches. That's the margin they're working with.",
